                                                "sense_id": "7631a94c-a1a1-3b25-96b1-1e2ece84ea93",
                                                "text": "These results indicate reduviids, and possibly other fast-feeding solenophagous arthropods like sandflies, provoke a weak immune response initially, but macroscopic reactions develop quickly once appropriate sensitization occurs as a result of chronic exposure."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4dec668-1ecc-4362-af6b-01e438637d40",
                                                "sense_id": "7631a94c-a1a1-3b25-96b1-1e2ece84ea93",
                                                "text": "Mosquitoes, fleas, lice, and bloodsucking bugs, whose mouthparts are long and well adapted to localize blood vessels and suck directly from them or from pools formed by their rupture, are called solenophagous."
                                            }
